# FORBIDDEN: `!important`

**Hard ban. No exceptions for AI/agent tasks. No “just this once.”**

## Rule

1. **Never write `!important`** in any stylesheet (`.scss`, `.css`, component styles, global overrides, theme files).
2. **Never introduce `!important` to “win” against Angular Material, themes, or legacy CSS.** That is a cascade/architecture failure — fix specificity, tokens, or selector ownership instead.
3. **Before starting any UI/style task**, confirm this rule. If an existing file still contains `!important`, do not add more; prefer removing nearby ones when touching that code.
4. **If a style does not apply without `!important`**, stop and fix the real cause:
   - wrong selector / theme attribute (`html[data-theme]` vs `body`)
   - Material CSS variables (`--mdc-*`, `--mat-*`) instead of fighting painted properties
   - load order / wrong layer (component vs `overrides/` vs theme)
   - encapsulation — move Material chrome overrides to `src/styles/overrides/` with higher specificity (repeat classes), not `!important`

## Correct patterns

```scss
/* Win with tokens Material already reads */
.mat-mdc-icon-button {
  --mdc-icon-button-hover-state-layer-opacity: 0;
  --mat-icon-button-state-layer-color: transparent;
}

/* Win with specificity (no !important) */
[data-theme='dark-glass'] .admin-header.mat-toolbar .mat-mdc-icon-button.mat-mdc-button-base {
  border-radius: 50%;
  background-color: transparent;
}
```

## Forbidden

```scss
.my-button {
  background: transparent !important; /* NEVER */
}
```

